{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"A4-2 narrowed `prev_snapshot.json` to a key set. For a key present in both snapshots, `_compute_mutations_emit_both` receives `local_fields = {}` and populated Jira fields. The current loop turns that into a non-empty mapping such as `{\"summary\": null}`, so the existing `if changed:` guard still emits a phantom outbound update.\n\nA4-1 is already merged as Gerrit 1256, commit `6cdd4b00d9ee`, with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. It drops this `field_drift` emission immediately after `compute_mutations`, before dispatch. A4-3 removes the phantom earlier at the differ seam so the pure mutation output is honest; the downstream zero-mutation and zero-git-call behavior is retained as regression coverage rather than attributed to this change. Research evidence remains in session log `1cb6-d553-6565-49b4`.\n\n## Approach\n\nReturn early from `_compute_mutations_emit_both` when `local_fields` is empty, before computing `changed`. This is the exact key-set gate. Do not test `changed` for emptiness: with `local_fields = {}` and `jira_fields = {\"summary\": \"remote\"}`, `changed` is `{\"summary\": None}`. Preserve the existing emission for genuine local data such as `{\"summary\": \"local\"}` versus `{\"summary\": \"remote\"}`. Keep the A4-1 downstream suppression unchanged as defense in depth.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An empty local entry from a key-set previous snapshot emits zero branch-3 outbound updates. Tier: focused `compute_mutations` unit test seen RED first plus the committed corpus script.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A genuine non-empty local payload still emits the same outbound update. Tier: unit negative control.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A converged pass records `mutation_count == 0`. Tier: integration regression control already established by A4-1.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A converged pass performs exactly zero per-mutation `git rev-parse` calls; a positive control proves the counting shim observes a representative call. Tier: integration regression control.\n\n## Files\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py`, focused tests, and `docs/experiments/keyset_prev_snapshot_corpus.py`.\n\nScope: S. Depends on closed A4-2."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785773990671202001,"uuid":"edbff364-98a1-4478-ba16-a18d7fe581f9"}